quill — https://github.com/digimata/quill
MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 Andrew Jones.

Portions of Sources/MeetingsCore/Audio/MicRecorder.swift are derived from
quill's Sources/quill/Audio/MicRecorder.swift — specifically the AVAudioEngine
voice-processing graph (the duplex render path VoiceProcessingIO requires, the
single explicit mono client format on both sides of the unit, the "other audio"
ducking configuration) and the first-second silence liveness check that falls
back to raw capture. Adapted here to write 16 kHz mono WAV rather than AAC.

EngineSegment.grouped(words:) in
Sources/MeetingsCore/Transcription/TranscriptionEngine.swift is derived from
quill's ParakeetEngine.segments(from:) — grouping word timings into readable
segments by sentence-ending punctuation, silence gap and a hard length cap.

The zero-frame probe in
Sources/MeetingsCore/Transcription/FluidAudioBatchEngine.swift follows quill's
guard in ParakeetEngine.transcribe(_:), and for the same reason: a track with no
frames makes AVFoundation raise an Objective-C exception inside the resampler
that Swift cannot catch, taking the whole process down.

